    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nDimensionActivity.onCreate invokes android.webkit.WebView.setWebContentsDebuggingEnabled(true), and the invocation is controlled by Version.isLollipop rather than an effective development/debug-build predicate in the complete reviewed method. This satisfies the rule's static unguarded-production-candidate condition; it does not establish deployed release execution.\r\n\r\nKeep any WebView-debugging enablement control-dependent on an effective development/debug-build predicate, using the Android-documented development-only semantics, while preserving the existing supported-platform condition where it remains relevant. This addresses the static candidate without relying on undocumented detector behavior.\r\n\r\nChanges:\r\n\r\n- `app/src/main/java/com/hiddenramblings/tagmo/wave9/DimensionActivity.kt`: Imports the module BuildConfig needed to restrict WebView debugging to debug builds; Enables WebView debugging only for debug builds, within the existing Lollipop-only branch.\r\n\r\n## How was this tested?\r\n\r\n- No automated test was added in this change\r\n- [x] Project compiles successfully (`assembleDebug`)\r\n\r\n## Additional context\r\n\r\nI’m an undergraduate Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), and this contribution is part of a research project involving static analysis of Android apps.\r\n\r\nI’m happy to adjust the implementation to better match the project’s architecture, coding conventions, or maintainers’ recommendations.",
